 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? They're a great starting point. Audio dramas and short stories that finish in under thirty minutes are perfect. Then nature stories and shows with animals are perfect. Try the BBC's Natural History podcast. Most of them are. Ratings on each episode help too. Yes, and usually a short summary too. Ask her to choose a rating before she starts, so she's involved too. At first, with you nearby, so she knows where to stop if she starts to worry. She probably will. Let me know if you need more tips.",
